---
/**
 * Required on every article. We write about incentives, utilities and land
 * transactions, none of which we are licensed to advise on.
 *
 * Marked data-boilerplate so the duplicate copy checker skips it. This is a
 * legal notice rather than editorial prose, and it has to read identically on
 * every domain: a disclaimer reworded eighteen ways to satisfy a search engine
 * is a worse disclaimer, and the wording is the part doing the work.
 *
 * That attribute still must not go anywhere near article or page copy. If body
 * text repeats across sites, the fix is to write different text.
 */
---

<aside class="disclaimer" data-boilerplate>
  <p>
    This article is general information, not legal, tax, or financial advice.
    Programs and rules change. Confirm anything that matters to your decision
    with your own attorney or accountant before you act on it.
  </p>
</aside>

<style>
  .disclaimer {
    margin: var(--s6) 0;
    padding: var(--s4) var(--s5);
    background: var(--surface-sunken);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--rule-strong);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius) var(--radius) 0;
  }

  .disclaimer p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }
</style>
